        "findings": "VERDICT: CHANGES REQUESTED\n\nThe membership-level logic itself is factored well: `hasTenureBonus(Owner)` mirrors the existing `hasEmail(Owner)` predicate, sits immediately below its caller, and keeps `toMembershipLevel` reading as a clean sequence of `if (...) level++;` steps. That is the right unit and the right shape.\n\nOne idiomatic inconsistency:\n\n- `OwnerMapper.java:188` references `java.time.temporal.ChronoUnit.DAYS` by its fully-qualified name inline. Every other `java.time` type in this file is imported at the top (`import java.time.LocalDate;`, `import java.time.Period;`) and used by simple name. A maintainer would expect `ChronoUnit` to follow suit: add `import java.time.temporal.ChronoUnit;` and use `ChronoUnit.DAYS.between(registrationDate, LocalDate.now())`. As written, the fully-qualified inline reference reads as out of place against the surrounding convention."
